  - polymer composites
  - machine learning
  - materials informatics
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  Code for the Dravix engine, which maps a polymer formulation (base polymer, additives with role
  and amount, heat flux, specimen thickness) to cone-calorimeter time to ignition, peak heat
  release rate, total heat released and average heat release rate. It also contains the scripts,
  pre-declared experiment configs, independent critic reviews and run logs for a literature
  cone-calorimeter benchmark (repeated random and paper-grouped 5-fold cross-validation). See
  BENCHMARK.md for the protocol and for which numbers are held-out evidence. Developed with
  substantial help from AI coding agents (Anthropic Claude); the authors are responsible for the
  content. A screening aid, not for fire-safety certification.
